    {
      "title": "Samsung keeps shattering profit records as AI boom lifts chip demand",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/world-news/samsung-keeps-shattering-profit-records-as-ai-boom-lifts-chip-demand-126102900116_1.html",
      "description": "Samsung Electronics said Thursday that its operating profit for the last quarter reached a record 107.4 trillion won (USD 80.5 billion), fuelled by surging demands for its computer memory chips used in artificial intelligence systems.\nRevenue for the July-September period rose to an all-time high at 195.3 trillion won (USD 146 billion), marking the company's fourth straight quarter of record profit and revenue.\nSamsung's regulatory filing came a day after domestic rival SK Hynix also reported record third-quarter profit, as the two South Korean semiconductor giants, which together control about two-thirds of the global memory market, face seemingly insatiable demand for their chips amid the global AI boom.\nSamsung said in a statement that it expects the demand for its AI-related chips to accelerate through 2027, outpacing supply as clients race to expand AI infrastructure. The company said it will focus on supplying advanced memory chips and storage products used in AI servers, ...",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-29T04:23:07"
